# Everything here is sent to the Docker daemon before the build starts, so
# keeping it small is the difference between a build that starts instantly and
# one that spends a minute uploading a build tree it is about to rebuild
# anyway.
#
# Two of these matter for more than speed: build/ carries SQLite databases from
# local testing — real accounts, password hashes, workspace files — and .env
# carries SESSION_SECRET. Neither belongs anywhere near an image that gets
# distributed.

# Local build trees. The image builds from source in its own stage.
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# Runtime state: databases, per-user workspaces, uploaded fonts.
data/

# Secrets and local configuration.
.env
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx

# The frontend's own git metadata; the files themselves are needed.
web/.git/
.git/
.gitmodules

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs and scratch output.
*.log
*.pack

# Documentation is not needed to compile or run the server.
README.md
